<title>USA: Fuel-Tech venture wins $1.5 mln contracts.</title>
<headline>Fuel-Tech venture wins $1.5 mln contracts.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fuel-Tech NV said Wednesday that Nalco Fuel Tech, its joint venture with Nalco Chemical Co, has been awarded three contracts valued at $1.5 million.</p>
<p>The company said the contracts, with a waste incineration company that it declined to identify, a boiler maker, and Nucor Corp, are all for products or intellectual property used in the reduction of harmful emissions.</p>
<p>Fuel-Tech develops and commercializes proprietary air pollution control technologies.</p>
</text>
